WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.158
Then the jolly ghost vanished, and a cold, dark creature in a black hood came toward Scrooge.

2
00:00:07.159 --> 00:00:11.453
Unlike the other ghosts, this one was not friendly.

3
00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:14.037
In fact, he had the look of death.

4
00:00:14.038 --> 00:00:19.253
"You must be the Ghost of Christmas Future," inquired Scrooge.

5
00:00:19.254 --> 00:00:23.529
But the ghost said nothing.

6
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:28.539
Pointing his bony finger, the ghost led Scrooge to a group of businessmen.

7
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.848
"I heard he died last night," said one man.

8
00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:35.863
"I wonder who will get his money?" joked another man.

9
00:00:35.864 --> 00:00:37.666
"He hasn't left it to me.

10
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:43.063
That's all I know," said the first man, and he walked off.

11
00:00:43.064 --> 00:00:47.058
"Why are you showing me this?" asked Scrooge.

12
00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:50.358
But still the black ghost said nothing.

13
00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:53.072
Then they went to a group of servants.

14
00:00:53.073 --> 00:00:56.421
"Since he's dead, he doesn't need this.

15
00:00:56.422 --> 00:01:00.915
Quick, let's each take something," declared one maid.

16
00:01:00.916 --> 00:01:08.286
"He doesn't have any friends to claim his things," she continued.

17
00:01:08.287 --> 00:01:14.601
"We worked in his miserable house, so we earned it," said another.

18
00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:22.432
Scrooge watched in disgust as the servants divided silver spoons and other expensive things among themselves.

19
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:31.821
Scrooge turned to the ghost saying, "I see! This could be me, if I do not change."

20
00:01:31.822 --> 00:01:36.426
The Ghost of Christmas Future took Scrooge to Bob Cratchit's house.

21
00:01:36.427 --> 00:01:39.299
This time there was less joy there.

22
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.422
"Did you visit Tiny Tim today, Father?" asked one of the children sadly.

23
00:01:44.423 --> 00:01:49.268
"Yes, and I brought some flowers for his grave," he replied.

24
00:01:49.269 --> 00:01:55.514
"It is beautiful there," said Bob with a tear.

25
00:01:55.515 --> 00:02:00.011
For the first time ever, Scrooge felt true sorrow in his heart.

26
00:02:00.012 --> 00:02:05.363
"Poor Bob," he thought. "He did love that boy."

27
00:02:05.364 --> 00:02:11.534
Then leaving that scene, Scrooge and the ghost traveled to a dreary graveyard.

28
00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:17.414
The spirit brought him to a grave where a coffin was being placed.

29
00:02:17.415 --> 00:02:20.921
There was no one there except a workman.

30
00:02:20.922 --> 00:02:25.966
Before Scrooge would look at the name on the new gravestone, he asked the ghost,

31
00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:34.319
"Spirit, tell me this, are these the things that will be or the things that might be?"

32
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.725
The ghost made no response.

33
00:02:38.726 --> 00:02:45.751
Scrooge continued, "But if a man changes, then surely his future changes, right?

34
00:02:45.752 --> 00:02:48.665
If not, why would you visit me?"

35
00:02:48.666 --> 00:02:51.446
The ghost pointed to the grave.

36
00:02:51.447 --> 00:02:56.134
There on the gravestone was his name, Ebenezer Scrooge.

37
00:02:56.135 --> 00:03:00.654
With a loud cry, Scrooge declared, "This is not I.

38
00:03:00.655 --> 00:03:07.867
I am not this lonely man. No!

39
00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:13.588
I will honor Christmas in my heart, and try to keep it all the year.

40
00:03:13.589 --> 00:03:17.806
I will live in the past, the present, and the future.

41
00:03:17.807 --> 00:03:20.501
I will love others and help the poor.

42
00:03:20.502 --> 00:03:24.853
Please, give me another chance," pleaded Scrooge.

43
00:03:24.854 --> 00:03:31.552
At that, the dark ghost faded away in a puff of smoke.

44
00:03:31.553 --> 00:03:37.456
Scrooge found himself back in his bedroom. It was a bright, crisp morning.

45
00:03:37.457 --> 00:03:41.286
He was alive, and a completely new man.

46
00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:49.165
He opened his window and shouted to a boy walking along the street, "My good boy, what day is it today?"

47
00:03:49.166 --> 00:03:55.798
"Why, it is Christmas," replied the puzzled boy.

48
00:03:55.799 --> 00:04:00.520
"Excellent!" shouted Scrooge. "I haven't missed it.

49
00:04:00.521 --> 00:04:06.896
My good boy, do you know the shop that has the very big turkey in its window?" asked Scrooge.

50
00:04:06.897 --> 00:04:09.649
"Of course," responded the boy.

51
00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:15.211
"An intelligent boy! Go and buy it, and bring it here," said Scrooge.

52
00:04:15.212 --> 00:04:21.659
"Come back in less than five minutes, and I'll give you half a crown!"

53
00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.010
The boy was off like a shot.

54
00:04:24.011 --> 00:04:28.708
"I'll send it to Bob Cratchit's!" laughed Scrooge.

55
00:04:28.709 --> 00:04:33.059
"He won't know who sent it. It's twice the size of Tiny Tim."

56
00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:39.901
Then Scrooge dressed himself in his best clothes and went to visit his nephew.

57
00:04:39.902 --> 00:04:44.267
Before he could change his mind, he ran up and knocked on the door.

58
00:04:44.268 --> 00:04:48.275
"Uncle Scrooge?" said his nephew with great surprise.

59
00:04:48.276 --> 00:04:56.411
"If you are willing to have me, I'd like to dine with you tonight," said Scrooge.

60
00:04:56.412 --> 00:05:01.673
Scrooge's nephew almost shook his hand off because he was so pleased.

61
00:05:01.674 --> 00:05:05.927
Never did Scrooge have so much fun as he did that day.

62
00:05:05.928 --> 00:05:10.011
He ate and talked like he had never done before.

63
00:05:10.012 --> 00:05:15.453
After that Christmas Day, Scrooge became a different man.

64
00:05:15.454 --> 00:05:19.514
To Bob Cratchit, he became a wonderful employer.

65
00:05:19.515 --> 00:05:27.313
Bob's family suffered no more, and Scrooge provided money to help Tiny Tim, who did not die.

66
00:05:27.314 --> 00:05:31.622
In the city, he became known for his kindness and friendship.

67
00:05:31.623 --> 00:05:36.247
He put his money toward work to help the poor and suffering.

68
00:05:36.248 --> 00:05:39.012
He never saw the ghosts again.

69
00:05:39.013 --> 00:05:45.045
From that day on, it was always said of him that he knew how to keep Christmas well.

70
00:05:45.046 --> 00:05:54.624
May that be said of all of us! And as Tiny Tim said, "God bless everyone."

